    <mxCell id="Ares" value="Result: cloud shows 1 (or 2)&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-size:12px;margin-top:4px&quot;&gt;Whichever till arrives last wins, so the cloud says &lt;b&gt;1&lt;/b&gt; (or 2 if the order flips).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;True on-hand: &lt;b&gt;5 − 3 − 4 + 10 = 8&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The +10 receipt was silently overwritten, and the count is off by 7. Nobody gets an error: the data is just wrong, and every report and reorder built on it is wrong too.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=4;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FBE3E3;strokeColor=#C94545;strokeWidth=1.8;fontColor=#1A1A1A;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=34;spacingTop=8;spacingRight=8;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DJetBrains%2BMono;" vertex="1" parent="1">
